# Local development & verification deps. The production Docker image only
# installs requirements.txt; this file is for developer machines so `make
# done` can run lint/format/type/test/coverage and the Playwright suites.
#
# Dev tools live in their own lockfile so the prod image doesn't carry
# ruff/mypy/pytest. Install both on a developer machine:
#
#   pip install -r requirements.txt -r requirements-dev.txt
#
# Re-lock with:
#   pip-compile --output-file=requirements.txt requirements.in
#   pip-compile --output-file=requirements-dev.txt requirements-dev.in

# boto3 is what scripts/lightsail_access.py uses to mint the short-lived SSH
# key pair for the mention-bot box, so no durable server key is ever written
# down. It belongs HERE rather than in requirements.in: the fly.io image
# installs only requirements.txt, and the Lightsail box itself installs only
# websockets + configobj, so neither of them should carry an AWS SDK. A session
# that cannot import boto3 cannot deploy or even check the deployed bot -
# caught 2026-08-31, when a fresh container had to pip-install it by hand.
boto3
mypy
pip-tools
playwright
pytest
pytest-cov
pytest-xdist
ruff
